From a7ab496e7e99f585507a0d4a08dbf1ae2eca1cba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arc-moe <arc-moe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:54:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] sycl: the pinned expert mirror in 1 GiB chunks; RAM kept
 free after it

The mirror was one sycl::malloc_host of every mirrored expert - 10.5 GB for
IQ2_XS on 2x A770. Arc A-series reports a max_mem_alloc_size of ~4 GB and
Level Zero's relaxed allocation limits cover device and shared memory only,
so the allocation failed, the mirror was empty, STRATA_VERIFY_NO_HOST=auto
turned off, and the next host allocation (the MTP drafter's load) ended the
engine with UR_RESULT_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY.

- GgufExpertSource::mirror allocates chunks of at most 1 GiB (and never
  above the device's max_mem_alloc_size), filled in profile order; a chunk
  the driver refuses only drops the mirror's coldest tail. Each mirrored
  expert has its own pointer instead of an offset into one base.
- STRATA_MIRROR_RESERVE_MIB (default 4096, as before): the RAM the mirror
  leaves free for what loads after it. setup_intel.py writes 8192: the MTP
  drafter reads its files into RAM, then the image encoder and the server.
